{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the $4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02712 (EV-FARE-02712, cancellation_fee $4.50, total_charged $4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd $0.00) is refunded in full to the rider. No driver compensation is paid.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. POL-NS-01 requires all four limbs. Limbs (a) and (d) are recorded: the trip record carries the driver's arrival event at 12:30:36 and a driver termination at 12:34:59 coded RIDER_NO_SHOW (one of the three codes limb (d) recognises). But limb (b) and limb (c) fail. This is a LARGE_VENUE pickup (EV-TRIP-02712, pickup_zone_class LARGE_VENUE), so the POL-NS-02 arrival radius is 120 m, not 50 m, and the driver's own trace (EV-GPS-02712) never places him inside it: his closest approach to the pin is 258.2 m (derived.driver_track.min_distance_m), the qualifying in-radius fix count is 0, and the longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0.0 s. Limb (c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the 'I'm Here' tap, and against the 180 s free waiting period in force (EV-TRIP-02712, platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180) the shortfall is 180 s. POL-NS-06 makes the fee not chargeable on that shortfall alone, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she replied to messages.\n\nThe driver advocate's 263-second argument (claim 3, and the shortfall being 'a measurement of position, not of time allowed') is answered on its own terms and rejected as a ground for keeping the fee: the 263 s runs from 12:30:36 to 12:34:59, it is the time the driver allowed, and limb (c) does not measure from the button press. The driver's closest approach (258.2 m) sits outside the 120 m radius but inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling, so POL-NS-03 independently refunds in full — he did not arrive at the pickup point. Both routes (POL-NS-02 for a trace with no in-radius fix at all, POL-NS-03 for a stationary position within 400 m) end in the same full refund, and the driver advocate properly concedes the fee is not chargeable.\n\nWhy there is no driver payment. POL-NS-07 pays 80% of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full; limb (b) fails and POL-NS-06 independently displaces the fee. POL-NS-03 puts the loss on the driver for compensation purposes: the rider stated a specific sub-location in the chat log at 12:30:56 ('im at the main entrance next to the taxi stand, block A', EV-CHAT-02712) and the driver did not move to it before cancelling at 12:34:59. The pin-ambiguity goodwill of $2.25 (POL-NS-03(ii)) is unavailable because trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, not 2 or more, and because the rider did specify a sub-location. The driver's anti-farming position (claim 5) is correct as far as it goes — no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against completed_trips_30d of 92, so neither limb of the POL-NS-07 check trips, and those are the only profile fields POL-GEN-01 permits for that test — but it changes nothing, because no compensation route is reached.\n\nThe rider's POL-NS-04 point is not needed and does not carry her case: the driver replied 'ok' at 12:31:26, within 120 seconds of the rider's 12:30:56 message, so the clause does not exonerate her on driver non-response. Her presence is in fact affirmatively established (54 qualifying rider fixes, never more than 19.9 m from the pin, well inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius), which contradicts the RIDER_NO_SHOW label, but the refund follows from the driver's own trace under POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 regardless. Her point that the 12:30:36 event is a driver-pressed marker is accepted: arrival_marker is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO, so POL-NS-12 does not convert that tap into a platform-confirmed arrival. I do not record a false-arrival referral under POL-NS-05(ii): that referral requires the GPS to place the driver more than 300 m from the pin at the arrival timestamp or moving at 15 km/h or more, and a closest approach of 258.2 m establishes neither, so no clause-mandated referral fires here.\n\nConfidence and effect. The facts the ruling rests on are carried by EV-GPS-02712, EV-TRIP-02712 and EV-CHAT-02712, all COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and the $4.50 fare line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so no POL-NS-08 limb (a)–(d) fires and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger holds; confidence is 0.9, above the 0.70 floor. The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02712-01 (weight 0.0) carries no fact relied on here. The monetary effect ($4.50) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00, so this provisional ruling executes automatically on issue, subject to appeal under POL-GEN-04. Two rider claims that relied on the weight-0.0 advisory without disclosing its MISSING_ARTIFACT impairment were discarded by the referee and are recorded in the audit below."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The missing dwell cannot be topped up by summing separate in-geofence intervals: POL-NS-06 limb (i) permits that only where a traffic_advisory is present and populated and carries a type of KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT. EV-ADVIS-02712-01 is MISSING, has a null payload and carries weight 0.0, so limb (i) is unavailable, the zero dwell stands, and no exculpation can be built on that absent artifact.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02712-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The record is clean enough to decide without escalation: EV-TRIP-02712, EV-GPS-02712, EV-CHAT-02712 and EV-FARE-02712 are all COMPLETE at weight 1.0, the trace has 100 percent coverage with no gaps and a 10 s cadence, the chat sequence and read receipts are intact, and the $4.50 cancellation line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so POL-NS-08 limbs (a) to (d) fire nowhere. No POL-NS-09 trigger holds either: no counter-party disputes are recorded on either profile, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and the driver's single no_show_termination in 30 days against 92 completed trips is nowhere near the POL-NS-07 anti-farming threshold.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02712-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
